    code: "PRJ-033",
    name: "Automatic Segregation Bio-medical Safety System",
    description: "Biomedical waste segregation is essential to prevent infection and contamination. This project uses AI, computer vision, and Arduino to identify medical waste such as needles, glass, and cotton, then automatically opens the correct disposal bin using servo motors. The system improves safety, hygiene, and reduces human intervention.\\n\\n**Status**: Biomedical waste management is a critical issue in healthcare environments due to the risks of infection and contamination caused by improper segregation of hazardous materials such as needles, glass, and cotton. Manual handling of such waste exposes healthcare workers to dangerous conditions and increases the chances of disease transmission. To address this problem, this project proposes an AI Powered Smart Healthcare Waste Segregation System that integrates computer vision and machine learning with an Arduino-based embedded system. A camera captures images of the waste, and a trained AI model classifies the objects into predefined categories, after which the classification result is sent to the Arduino to control servo motors that automatically open the appropriate disposal bin, enabling touchless and accurate segregation. The system is cost-effective, efficient, and reduces human intervention while improving safety and hygiene in medical environments. Furthermore, it has the potential for future enhancements such as improved AI accuracy, real-time processing, and IoT-based monitoring, making it a scalable solution for modern healthcare waste management.   give this upto 350 letters  Abstract (within ~350 characters):  Biomedical waste segregation is essential to prevent infection and contamination. This project uses AI, computer vision, and Arduino to identify medical waste such as needles, glass, and cotton, then automatically opens the correct disposal bin using servo motors. The system improves safety, hygiene, and reduces human intervention.     Today 2:56 PM Give abstract for this   Here's a simple and concise abstract (around 180–200 words) suitable for a mini project report:  Abstract  Biomedical waste management is an important part of healthcare because improper disposal of medical waste can spread infections and harm the environment. This project presents an AI-Powered Smart Healthcare Waste Segregation System that automatically identifies and separates biomedical waste using artificial intelligence and an Arduino-based control system. A camera captures the image of the waste item, and a trained AI model classifies it into categories such as needles, glass, or cotton. Based on the classification result, the Arduino controls a servo motor to open the appropriate waste bin automatically. This touchless process reduces direct human contact with hazardous waste, improving the safety of healthcare workers and maintaining better hygiene. The system is low-cost, easy to implement, and suitable for hospitals, clinics, and laboratories. It also minimizes errors in waste segregation and supports efficient biomedical waste management. In the future, the system can be enhanced with IoT technology for real-time monitoring and advanced AI models for higher classification accuracy. Overall, this project provides a smart, reliable, and scalable solution for safer and more efficient biomedical waste disposal in healthcare environments.\\n\\n**Repository**: [GitHub Link](https://github.com/suji187cf-pixel/AUTOMATIC-SEGREGATION-BIOMEDICAL-SAFETY-SYSTEM)",
